# SYN-OS's default apps on the Arch stream: what xdg-open (and so
# SYN-SHELL, the browser, Steam and the bar) opens each kind of file and
# link with, for every user. ~/.config/mimeapps.list overrides it; that's
# what Preferences > Desktop > Default Apps (syn-pipe-defaults.zsh)
# writes, and its "Reset to SYN-OS default" falls back to this file.
#
# Generated with `syn-pipe-defaults.zsh --types CATEGORY APP` for each
# line of the table below: every type the app opens in the category, and
# every alias of each (a WAV is audio/vnd.wave, audio/wav and audio/x-wav).
# PDFs are left out: nothing on the package list views them.
#
#   web        org.kde.falkon.desktop     archives   syn-shell.desktop
#   files      syn-shell.desktop          text       featherpad.desktop
#   images     feh.desktop                audio      vlc.desktop
#   video      vlc.desktop
[Default Applications]
